DESCRIPTION:Mummy Luminaries from 1 to 4:30 p.m.\nPaynetown SRA\, Activity 
 Center\n\n•    Cost is $5 per project (cash or check only).\n•    Supp
 lies are limited\; first-come first-served!\n•    Recommended for ages 8
  and up.\n\nDROP BY to make a Mummy Luminary - the perfect Halloween acces
 sory for your campsite picnic table\, patio table\, or fireplace mantle! W
 ith an eerie green glow and glow-in-the-dark eyes\, this quart-sized glass
  luminary is easy to assemble (and we’ll give you a green votive candle\
 , so you can use it right away). Craft takes 15 to 20 minutes to complete.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center
SUMMARY:Mummy Luminaries\, Paynetown SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/mummy-luminaries-paynetown-sra-mo
 nroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261121T064838Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54028327541417
DTSTART:20261106T150000Z
DTEND:20261106T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Virtual Program: “What Remains: The Monroe Reservoir Cemetery
  Relocation Project” at 10:00 a.m.\n\nThis program will be presented LIV
 E on Facebook at tinyurl.com/cemeteryrelocation2026\, with a question-and-
 answer session offered at the conclusion of the program. Mark yourself as 
 “going” to receive a reminder about 10 minutes prior to the program’
 s start! If you are unable to view the program live\, a recording will be 
 available on the Reels tab of Monroe Lake’s Facebook page later in the d
 ay.\n\nIn 1960\, the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (USACE) was tasked with 
 building a reservoir that would impact almost 50\,000 acres in the Salt Cr
 eek Valley of south-central Indiana. This endeavor would necessitate the u
 prooting of thousands of people currently residing on the land. But it was
 n’t just the living that had to be moved.\n\nThis is the story of how 7 
 cemeteries\, consisting of 335 burials\, were disinterred for the construc
 tion of Monroe Lake – and how they were reburied with the intent of pres
 erving both cemetery history and family connections to the Salt Creek Vall
 ey. \n\nPlease note that Monroe Lake has a public Facebook page. This mean
 s that a Facebook account is not required to watch either the live program
  or the recording\; however\, an account is required if you wish to ask qu
 estions or post comments on the video.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, VIRTUAL presentation at http://tinyurl.com/cemeteryr
 elocation2026
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: VIRTUAL PROGRAM - "What Remains: The Monroe Re
 servoir Cemetery Relocation Project" (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-virtual-progr
 am-what-remains-the-monroe-reservoir-cemetery-relocation-project
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261121T064838Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54028367184188
DTSTART:20261107T183000Z
DTEND:20261107T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Elkinsville History Tour at 1:30 p.m.\n\n•    Sign up at tiny
 url.com/elkinsville2025 \n•    Registration required by November 3.\n•
     Cost is $10 per person.\n•    Limited to 15 people\; recommended for
  ages 14 and up.\n•    Location: Meet at the Story Inn parking lot in St
 ory\, IN\n\nJoin us for a tour through the “town that was!” Prior to t
 he construction of Monroe Lake\, Elkinsville was a center of commerce and 
 community for a remote part of Brown County. Explore the history of this t
 own\, walk its former main street\, visit the cemetery\, and find out what
  happened to this community after the lake went in. 2 hrs 30 min (approx.)
 \n\nAll registrations are final. No refunds will be offered\, unless the t
 our itself is cancelled. You may transfer an existing reservation to anoth
 er person by contacting Jill Vance at jvance@dnr.in.gov at least 2 days pr
 ior to the tour.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Meets at Story Inn parking lot in Story\, IN (ignore
  S.R. 446 address\; directions will be emailed to registered attendees)
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Elkinsville History Tour (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-elkinsville-h
 istory-tour-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261121T064838Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54028422771879
DTSTART:20261107T230000Z
DTEND:20261108T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Southern Indiana Folk Songs at 6:00 p.m.\n\n•    Free program
  (donations accepted) and free park entry!\n•    Location: Paynetown Sta
 te Recreation Area\, Activity Center\n•    Please note that seating is l
 imited to 25 people\; we don’t expect the room to fill\, but we could al
 ways be surprised!\n\nFolk songs proliferated in an era when singing was a
  common form of recreation. People learned traditional folk songs by liste
 ning to others sing them and then passing them on to someone else. The Sal
 t Creek Valley\, where Monroe Lake now lies\, has a rich history of song\,
  heavily influenced by the people who moved here in the 1800s from the App
 alachian region. This program explores the history of folk music in southe
 rn Indiana and songs once sung right here in the valley\, including audio 
 recordings of local singers from the 1930s through 1980s.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Southern Indiana Folk Songs\, Paynetown SRA (M
 onroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-southern-indi
 ana-folk-songs-paynetown-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261121T064838Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54428698729284
DTSTART:20261212T183000Z
DTEND:20261212T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Winter Crafts Workshop at 1:30 p.m.\n\n•    Sign up by Decemb
 er 9 (click on "Buy Tickets" button).\n•    $10/person\, limited to 12 p
 eople.\n•    Recommended for ages 12 and up. \n•    Workshop Location:
  Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center\n\nJoin us for a relaxing afternoon of cr
 afting! Sip on hot cocoa or tea as you hand-paint a glass jar for a small 
 poured wax candle\, assemble a snowman ornament\, and make a set of Zentan
 gle gift tags with a winter theme. 60-75 minutes\n\nPlease note that all r
 egistrations are final. Refunds provided only if the workshop is cancelled
 .
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center
SUMMARY:Winter Crafts Workshop\, Paynetown SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/winter-crafts-workshop-paynetown-
 sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261121T064838Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54428774921967
DTSTART:20261221T121500Z
DTEND:20261221T131500Z
DESCRIPTION:Solstice Sunrise Run at 7:15 a.m.\n\n•    Sign up by December
  17 (click on "Register" button). \n•    FREE\, limited to 30 people.\n
 •    Meeting Location: Paynetown SRA\, Marina parking area (just past be
 ach)\n\nUsher in the winter solstice with a pre-dawn group run\, ending ju
 st in time to sip hot cocoa while we enjoy the sunrise together! The 3-mil
 e route is on park roads\; participants should be able to comfortably run 
 a 10:30 min/mile pace. Bring a headlamp or small hand-held flashlight.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Marina parking area
SUMMARY:Solstice Sunrise Run\, Paynetown SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/solstice-sunrise-run-paynetown-sr
 a-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
